# Pureweight Gold Exchange — environment
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. Never commit `.env.local`.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SITE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used for canonical URLs, Open Graph, the sitemap and robots.txt.
# Must be the production origin, with no trailing slash.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.pureweight.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE KEEPER'S TARGET REPOSITORY  (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which repo the Keeper commits content to. Defaults to
# proworkspaceofficial-bot/pw.main when unset, so a deploy that forgets this
# still works.
#
# It exists because the original owner account, pureweightofficial, was lost on
# 2026-09-02 — its only email was a Gmail address Google closed, and it had no
# 2FA, so no recovery route was open. Moving the Keeper to the new repo used to
# mean editing src/lib/keeper/github.ts and cutting a release. It is now a
# setting, so the next account move is a dashboard change instead.
#
# Read at BUILD time and inlined into the client bundle: changing it requires a
# redeploy, not a restart. The token you sign in with must have Contents: read
# and write on whatever you name here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_KEEPER_REPO=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE KEEPER'S SIGN-IN  (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# With these set, /keeper asks for an email and a password instead of a pasted
# GitHub token, and reads the token from Supabase after sign-in. Without them
# it falls back to the token screen exactly as before — a missing variable can
# never lock the owner out.
#
# Set them in Vercel (Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables) and in
# .env.local for local work. Both are NEXT_PUBLIC_, so both are compiled into
# the published JavaScript. That is expected: Supabase's anon key is designed
# to be public and is NOT the security boundary.
#
# ROW LEVEL SECURITY IS THE BOUNDARY. Run docs/supabase-keeper.sql before
# putting a real GitHub token in the database. Without those policies the anon
# key alone would read it.
#
# NEVER put the service_role key here, in any NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable, or
# anywhere the build can reach. It bypasses RLS entirely.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VALUATION ENQUIRY DELIVERY  —  NO LONGER USED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HISTORICAL. The valuation form, its API route and this delivery path were
# removed when the funnel became "call, or come in" — the business buys over
# the counter, and a form that produces a provisional figure added a step
# between the visitor and the counter rather than removing one. These two
# variables are read by nothing. They are kept here only so that anyone who
# finds them already set in a dashboard knows they can be deleted.
# Without this, POST /api/valuation returns 503 in production and tells the
# visitor to telephone instead. That is deliberate: a form that reports success
# while writing to a log nobody reads loses real enquiries silently.
#
# Point this at anything that accepts a JSON POST — Zapier, Make, n8n, a CRM
# intake endpoint, or your own API. See the payload shape in
# src/app/api/valuation/route.ts.
VALUATION_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Optional. Sent as `Authorization: Bearer <secret>` so the receiver can verify
# the request actually came from this site.
VALUATION_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
